                <pb facs="0214" n="98" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg98"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.51/486.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé
                            d’Affaires to the Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Extract.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1911-06-27">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 27, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I am informed that the French Chargé d’Affaires here has received a telegram from
                    his Government today stating that the Russian and Japanese Embassies at Paris
                    have protested against the sixteenth article of the currency-reform contract,
                    and ask the French Government to seek a revision of this article by the
                    Chinese.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Heintzleman</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
